1️⃣ What is HashMap?

HashMap is a Map implementation in Java.
Stores key-value pairs.
Keys are unique, values can be duplicate.
Does not maintain any order (insertion order is not preserved).
Allows 1 null key and multiple null values.

Internally implemented using hash table → buckets + linked list/tree (Java 8).

✅ Key idea: Fast access by key using hashing


✅ Notice: order is not preserved — HashMap is unordered.

4️⃣ HashMap Internals (Java 8+)

HashMap stores entries in buckets based on hashCode of key.
Each bucket initially is a linked list.
If bucket size > 8, linked list converted to Red-Black Tree for faster lookup (O(log n)).
Key equality is checked using equals().

5️⃣ HashMap vs LinkedHashMap vs TreeMap

Feature	     HashMap	 LinkedHashMap	    TreeMap
Key Order	   No	        Insertion	    Sorted (natural/comparator)
Null Key	   ✅ 1	         ✅ 1	        ❌ No
Null Values	   ✅	         ✅	            ✅
Performance	  O(1) avg	   O(1) avg	        O(log n)
Use-case	General 	 Maintain order	    Sorted map